  "scientific_notes": [
    "Each annual observation uses one selected August Landsat scene.",
    "The AOI is a fixed 400 x 400 pixel grid at 30 m resolution.",
    "QA water classification is not independent ground truth.",
    "NDWI and MNDWI thresholds are not universal water-classification thresholds.",
    "The strong post-2021 disagreement between NDWI and MNDWI prevents reliable water-area interpretation.",
    "Landsat 8 and Landsat 9 observations occur in different years and dates; their grouping is not a controlled sensor calibration.",
    "The 2018 observation has 6.3838 percent QA-invalid pixels.",
    "The fixed 2021 water-candidate pixel analysis measures spectral change at fixed locations; it does not prove shoreline movement.",
    "The OSM coastline is a provisional locator, not independent ground truth.",
    "Water-index changes can be affected by water level, season, wind, turbidity, sediment, land cover and sensor differences.",
    "No confirmed shoreline retreat is established by this dataset."
  ],
